  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating the mean difference from a reference point (zero), using both outcome magnitudes and probabilities. The individual mentions both probabilities and outcome magnitudes (size of loss), which are components of the reason. However, they do not compute or refer to a weighted average or expected difference from a reference point. Instead, they compare probability and outcome separately, and their comparison is factually incorrect (they reverse the probabilities). There is no indication they computed a mean difference or used the reference point systematically. While they consider some of the same inputs (loss size and probability), they do not apply the rule of the decision reason. The justification is based on a flawed qualitative trade-off, not the quantitative mean difference rule. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this specific decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
