  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reference value is zero, since neither lottery offers a sure outcome (100% probability), and thus the reference value defaults to zero. The differences between each outcome and the reference value are simply the outcomes themselves (i.e., -6000, 0 for Lottery A; -3000, 0 for Lottery B). The mean difference for each lottery is the expected value of these differences. For Lottery A: (-6000 * 0.45) + (0 * 0.55) = -2700. For Lottery B: (-3000 * 0.90) + (0 * 0.10) = -2700. Both lotteries have the same mean difference (-2700), so the decision reason would be indifferent between them.",
