{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reference value is zero, since there is no sure outcome (i.e., no outcome with 100% probability) in either lottery. The differences between each outcome and the reference value (zero) are simply the outcomes themselves: for Lottery A, -6000 and 0; for Lottery B, -3000 and 0. The mean difference for each lottery is calculated as the probability-weighted average of these differences. For Lottery A: (0.001 × -6000) + (0.999 × 0) = -6. For Lottery B: (0.002 × -3000) + (0.998 × 0) = -6. Both lotteries have the same mean difference (-6), so the decision reason would be indifferent between them.",
